,"triggered_by":null,"report_html":null},{"id":"MNT-0142-004","started_at":"2025-10-11T08:00:00Z","completed_at":"2025-10-11T15:00:00Z","type":"scheduled","equipment":"wellhead","issue":"Scheduled wellhead valve service","action":"Valves serviced and pressure tested","technician_id":"U-305","technician":"Megan Ward","contractor":null,"downtime_hours":7,"cost":846,"labor":422,"parts":424,"triggered_by":null,"report_html":null},{"id":"MNT-0142-005","started_at":"2025-12-27T08:00:00Z","completed_at":"2025-12-27T18:00:00Z","type":"scheduled","equipment":"pump_jack","issue":"Scheduled lubrication and belt inspection","action":"Lubricated, belts tensioned","technician_id":"U-303","technician":"Kevin Price","contractor":"Coyote Ridge Well Services","downtime_hours":10,"cost":575,"labor":274,"parts":301,"triggered_by":null,"report_html":null},{"id":"MNT-0142-006","started_at":"2026-03-29T08:00:00Z","completed_at":"2026-03-29T16:00:00Z","type":"scheduled","equipment":"wellhead","issue":"Scheduled wellhead valve service","action":"Valves serviced and pressure tested","technician_id":"U-303","technician":"Kevin Price","contractor":null,"downtime_hours":8,"cost":799,"labor":404,"parts":395,"triggered_by":null,"report_html":null},{"id":"MNT-0142-007","started_at":"2026-04-24T08:00:00Z","completed_at":"2026-04-25T02:00:00Z","type":"corrective","equipment":"flowline","issue":"Flowline leak causing spill","action":"Replaced leaking flowline section and remediated soil","technician_id":"U-305","technician":"Megan Ward","contractor":null,"downtime_hours":18,"cost":6510,"labor":2330,"parts":4180,"triggered_by":"INS-0142-0053","report_html":"<h1>Maintenance Report \u2014 MNT-0142-007</h1>\n<p><strong>Asset:</strong> WELL-0142 (NE-07 Well 142, T350, Northeast Block 7) <strong>Equipment:</strong> flowline <strong>Work started:</strong> 24 Apr 2026 08:00 \u00b7 <strong>Finished:</strong> 25 Apr 2026 02:00 \u00b7 <strong>Well stopped for this job:</strong> 18 hours <strong>Crew lead:</strong> Megan Ward (U-305) \u00b7 <strong>Crew:</strong> Daniel Foster <strong>Triggered by:</strong> inspection INS-0142-0053 on 2026-04-23 <strong>Report written:</strong> 26 Apr 2026</p>\n<h2>What happened</h2>\n<p>The weekly manual inspection INS-0142-0053 at 13:45 on 2026-04-23 found crude oil on the pad: about 1.0% of the pad area, estimated 0.5 bbl. The inspector noted: &quot;Staining along flowline route.&quot; The field operator shut the well in, closed the flowline valve and placed earth berms and absorbent pads. The release was contained about 1.3 hours after the inspection. The crew traced the leak to a corrosion hole along the flowline route.</p>\n<h2>Root cause</h2>\n<p>External corrosion where the pipe coating had been damaged.</p>\n<h2>Safety and permits</h2>\n<ul><li>Pre-job safety meeting held with the crew before work started (WS-01).</li><li>Energy isolated: prime mover stopped at the bottom of the stroke, brake set and chained, motor disconnect locked and tagged, wellhead wing valve closed and tagged, pressure bled off (WS-02).</li><li>Personal H2S monitors worn; highest reading 2 ppm, below the 10 ppm stop-work level (WS-03).</li><li>Hot work permit issued for welding; gas test before welding read 3% LEL, below the 10% limit (WS-04).</li></ul>\n<h2>Work done</h2>\n<ol><li>Excavated around the leak point.</li><li>Cut out the corroded section.</li><li>Welded in new line pipe.</li><li>Coated the new joints.</li><li>Excavated the stained soil.</li><li>Backfilled after the pressure test.</li></ol>\n<p>Summary of the fix: replaced leaking flowline section and remediated soil.</p>\n<h2>Testing and return to service</h2>\n<p>Pressure-tested the repaired section at 369 psi (1.25 \u00d7 the flowline&#x27;s maximum operating pressure of 295 psi) and held it for 4 hours with no pressure drop (WS-05). The well was returned to production.</p>\n<h2>Spill clean-up and waste</h2>\n<ul><li>About 0.5 m\u00b3 of stained soil excavated, bagged and sent to an approved disposal site under waste manifest WM-0142-007 (WS-06).</li><li>2 soil samples taken around the spill; the highest result after clean-up was 0.51% TPH, below the 1.0% target (SR-03).</li></ul>\n<h2>Parts and cost</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>USD</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Line pipe and fittings</td><td>1,881</td></tr><tr><td>Absorbents and berms</td><td>836</td></tr><tr><td>Soil hauling and disposal</td><td>1,463</td></tr><tr><td>Labour (company crew)</td><td>2,330</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td><strong>6,510</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Compliance check</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Protocol</th><th>Result</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>WS-01</td><td>Met</td><td>Meeting held and recorded</td></tr><tr><td>WS-02</td><td>Met</td><td>Energy isolated and tagged</td></tr><tr><td>WS-03</td><td>Met</td><td>Monitors bump-tested; highest 2 ppm</td></tr><tr><td>WS-04</td><td>Met</td><td>Permit issued; gas test 3% LEL</td></tr><tr><td>WS-05</td><td>Met</td><td>Tested at 1.25 \u00d7 maximum operating pressure, held 4 hours</td></tr><tr><td>WS-06</td><td>Met</td><td>Oily waste manifested to an approved site</td></tr><tr><td>WS-07</td><td>Met</td><td>Written 1 day after the work (limit 3 days)</td></tr><tr><td>SR-02</td><td>Met</td><td>Contained about 1.3 hours after discovery (limit 4 hours)</td></tr><tr><td>SR-04</td><td>Met</td><td>Spill recorded with volume and area (minor class)</td></tr><tr><td>SR-03</td><td>Met</td><td>Cleaned to below 1.0% TPH; agency verification applies only to reportable spills</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Notes and recommendations</h2>\n<ul><li>Inspect the remaining joints on this flowline.</li><li>Record the leak location for the flowline maintenance program (RC-05).</li></ul>"},{"id":"MNT-0142-008","started_at":"2026-05-22T08:00:00Z","completed_at":"2026-05-22T18:00:00Z","type":"scheduled","equipment":"wellhead","issue":"Scheduled wellhead valve service","action":"Valves serviced and pressure tested","technician_id":"U-305","technician":"Megan Ward","contractor":null,"downtime_hours":10,"cost":765,"labor":230,"parts":535,"triggered_by":null,"report_html":null},{"id":"MNT-0142-009","started_at":"2026-09-14T08:00:00Z","completed_at":"2026-09-14T18:00:00Z","type":"scheduled","equipment":"pump_jack","issue":"Scheduled lubrication and belt inspection","action":"Lubricated, belts tensioned","technician_id":"U-303","technician":"Kevin Price","contractor":null,"downtime_hours":10,"cost":304,"labor":131,"parts":173,"triggered_by":null,"report_html":null}],"context":[{"id":"CTX-0142-001","at":"2025-05-08T17:10:00Z","type":"correction","author_id":"U-401","author":"Laura Simmons","text":"Inspection INS-0142-0003: produced water from a washout, no crude. Not a crude spill.","inspection_id":"INS-0142-0003","valid_from":"2025-05-08","valid_to":null}],"regulatory":[],"unlinked_reports":[]}